Code Me Kya Ho Raha Hai? (backend/Dockerfile)
dockerfile
FROM node:20-alpine AS base         # 1. Ultra-lightweight Linux OS + Node.js 20
WORKDIR /app                       # 2. Container ke andar folder
COPY package*.json ./              
RUN npm ci --only=production       # 3. Sirf production libraries install karo
COPY . .                           # 4. Saara code copy karo
EXPOSE 5000                        # 5. Port 5000 open karo
CMD ["node", "server.js"]          # 6. Server start karo!
Kya Problem Solve Ki?
Environment Mismatch: Developer ke Windows aur server ke Ubuntu Linux me compatibility issue nahi hota.
Speed & Size: alpine Linux use karne se container ka size sirf 150MB banta hai (bina Docker ke full OS 1GB+ leta).
Interview Question & Answer:
Interviewer: "Why did you use Docker and Multi-Stage builds in your project?"
Your Answer: "Humne application consistency ke liye Docker use kiya. Frontend me humne Multi-stage Docker build use kiya — pehle stage me Node.js container ne React/Vite app compile ki, aur dusre stage me sirf compiled HTML/JS ko ultra-lightweight Nginx container me copy kar diya. Isse production image ka size 80% chhota ho gaya aur attack surface drastically reduce ho gaya."

2. Reverse Proxy & Web Server (Nginx)
Aasan Analogy: "Security Guard / Receptionist"
Agar koi guest building me aaye, toh wo seedha CEO ke cabin me nahi ghusta. Receptionist/Guard unhe milta hai, unka ID check karta hai, aur sahi room me bhejta hai.

Nginx wahi Guard/Receptionist hai:
Internet par public user sirf Port 80 (HTTP) ya Port 443 (HTTPS) se connect ho sakte hain. Hum apne backend Node.js (Port 5000) ko internet par directly open nahi karte (yeh insecure hota hai).

Humare Project Me Kahan Hai?


frontend/nginx.conf


